%S A398487 0,4,624,50018,2703376,108412740,3396389392,86201586889,1824247880960,
%T A398487 32960238759944,518502929641184,7218824265048208,90174409348191472,
%U A398487 1022374963077949504,10624053977856172288,102032984331144300154,912145051065012843856,7637267959754449187680,60212635580120294578320,449099088159314606776084
%N A398487 Number of unsatisfiable 3-SAT formulas with 4 variables and n clauses in the multiset clause model.
%C A398487 Clauses are multisets of 3 literals chosen from {x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4, not x_1, ..., not x_4}; repeated literals inside a clause are allowed. A formula is a multiset of n such clauses, so repeated clauses are also allowed.
%C A398487 This is row 4 of the array A396351; that is, a(n) = A396351(4,n). There are binomial(2*4+2,3) = binomial(10,3) = 120 clause types over 4 variables, so the total number of n-clause formulas is binomial(n+119,n), and a(n) is that total minus the number of satisfiable formulas A397492(4,n).
%D A398487 Stephen A. Cook, The complexity of theorem-proving procedures, Proceedings of the Third Annual ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing, 1971, 151-158.
%H A398487 <a href="/index/Rec#order_120">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, order 120.
%F A398487 a(n) = binomial(n+119,n) - A397492(4,n).
%F A398487 a(n) = binomial(n+119,n) - 16*binomial(n+99,n) + 32*binomial(n+89,n) + 48*binomial(n+83,n) + 32*binomial(n+80,n) - 88*binomial(n+79,n) + 24*binomial(n+75,n) - 192*binomial(n+73,n) - 128*binomial(n+70,n) + 256*binomial(n+69,n) - 48*binomial(n+67,n) + 240*binomial(n+66,n) - 288*binomial(n+65,n) + 384*binomial(n+63,n) - 192*binomial(n+62,n) + 208*binomial(n+61,n) + 208*binomial(n+60,n) - 544*binomial(n+59,n) + 512*binomial(n+58,n) + 32*binomial(n+57,n) - 952*binomial(n+56,n) + 492*binomial(n+55,n) - 576*binomial(n+54,n) - 512*binomial(n+53,n) + 1376*binomial(n+52,n) - 840*binomial(n+51,n) + 320*binomial(n+50,n) + 1360*binomial(n+49,n) - 1696*binomial(n+48,n) + 1168*binomial(n+47,n) + 192*binomial(n+46,n) - 1536*binomial(n+45,n) + 1344*binomial(n+44,n) - 564*binomial(n+43,n) - 1824*binomial(n+42,n) + 2640*binomial(n+41,n) - 576*binomial(n+40,n) - 1120*binomial(n+39,n) + 1504*binomial(n+38,n) - 216*binomial(n+37,n) - 1216*binomial(n+36,n) + 1000*binomial(n+35,n) - 288*binomial(n+34,n) + 64*binomial(n+33,n) - 32*binomial(n+32,n) + 7*binomial(n+31,n).
